===========================================
Information-theoretic structure:
===========================================
dim_F2 S^2(E_Hm/Q) = 4
S^2 contains image of E_Hm[2](Q) = (Z/2)^2 (full 2-torsion)
Image of 2-torsion has dim_F2 = 2 — that's S1 (= δ(order-8 generator)) and S2 (= δ(order-2 elt)).
Quotient S^2 / δ(E[2]) has dim_F2 = 2, generated by classes of Covers 3, 4.

By Cassels-Tate alternating pairing on S^2 / δ(E[2]) = Sha[2] + E(Q)/torsion image:
  CT is well-defined and alternating on a 2-dim F_2 space.
  Alternating on F_2^2: either identically zero, or matrix [[0,1],[1,0]] (rank 2).

Case A (CT trivial on Cov3, Cov4):
  Cov3, Cov4 could either ALL be in E(Q)/torsion image (=> rk = 2) OR all in Sha[2]
    (=> rk = 0, Sha[2] = (Z/2)^2 with CT identically 0 — BUT this contradicts
    CT being non-deg on Sha[2] by Cassels' theorem).
  Actually CT on Sha[2] is NON-DEGENERATE alternating; on a 2-dim Sha[2] it must be
    rank 2. So CT trivial => no Sha[2] above E(Q)-image => rk = 2.

Case B (CT non-trivial on Cov3, Cov4):
  Then S3, S4 are NOT both in E(Q) image => Sha[2] >= 2-dim. Combined with
    rk + dim Sha[2] = 2 => rk = 0, Sha[2] = (Z/2)^2.

CONCLUSION:
  CT(S3, S4) ≠ 0 (in F_2) ⟺ rk(E_Hm) = 0.
  This is exactly the missing computation we need.

Without correct S3, S4 triples we cannot compute this rigorously in PARI 2.15.4.
Magma's CasselsTatePairing function (or hand-coded local-invariant computation
on covers 3 and 4 with explicit local solubility witness) is required.

